/-
# Realizing finite BF4 vacuum-sector coefficients as dense linear observables

The arbitrary-carrier gap is stated for coefficient vectors on a finite
canonical vacuum component and their zero extensions to later cutoffs.  The
cutoff-removed physical completion, however, is generated by finite rational
linear combinations of globally bounded cylinder observables.  This module
identifies those two presentations.

For every state in a fixed finite vacuum component we construct its exact
lower-half cylinder indicator.  A finite rational linear combination of these
indicators is one literal `CentralPhysicalLinearObservable`.  On every later
positive carrier its coefficient vector is exactly the previously constructed
zero extension.  Consequently its finite physical norm and Markov quadratic
contract to the pulled vacuum-sector forms.

This is a dense-carrier realization theorem.  It does not prove that these
sector cylinders are dense in a completed vacuum sector, does not construct a
uniform all-carrier rate, and supplies no thermodynamic or continuum limit.

No `Classical.*`, choice, `native_decide`, `sorry`, custom axiom, or
noncomputable declaration.
-/

